# The Location Services check (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.loccheck): open the Privacy page by URL -- no taps --
# and leave the screen to the runner shots. The URL is one word (no spaces): the job parser splits
# words, and quotes around it are passed through, which is why the first attempt did nothing.
# With the system image that carries locationd (userland/system.apfs after the
# sysimage/select-system.py change), the page should offer Location Services.
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 150 &
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen prefs:root=Privacy&path=LOCATION
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen prefs:
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 60
